1
00:01:33,999 --> 00:01:36,840
I'm off! I'm off!

2
00:01:38,269 --> 00:01:41,020
Mokku, be careful out there.

3
00:01:41,716 --> 00:01:43,083
I know!

4
00:01:45,109 --> 00:01:49,120
He's really changed. He's become so dependable.

5
00:01:52,046 --> 00:01:55,551
Let's see... no, no.

6
00:01:57,099 --> 00:02:00,355
The folks in this village don't eat anything decent.

7
00:02:01,551 --> 00:02:08,793
Honestly... do they really want us to starve to death? Good grief... Huh?

8
00:02:08,914 --> 00:02:11,487
How mysterious...

9
00:02:12,519 --> 00:02:14,140
The scent of meat!

10
00:02:16,364 --> 00:02:18,342
You bastard!

11
00:02:18,944 --> 00:02:22,120
Trying to hog it all to yourself, you damn jerk!

12
00:02:22,900 --> 00:02:24,080
I wonder why.

13
00:02:24,720 --> 00:02:26,040
Oh, give me a break. Huh?

14
00:02:26,285 --> 00:02:27,420
Here comes Mokku.

15
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:31,600
Where do you think he's heading?

16
00:02:36,460 --> 00:02:40,410
Well, well, well, where are you off to, little Mokku?

17
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:46,100
Oh, Kenken. I'm going to town for Grandpa to order some new woodcarving tools.

18
00:02:46,405 --> 00:02:49,346
To town, huh? I wonder why...

19
00:02:49,370 --> 00:02:51,340
Maybe we should tag along with you?

20
00:02:51,655 --> 00:02:54,850
It's all right. I can go by myself. See you later!

21
00:02:55,405 --> 00:02:59,203
Hmph, he's gotten awfully cocky lately.

22
00:03:02,060 --> 00:03:05,170
Town, huh? Haven't been there in a while.

23
00:03:06,339 --> 00:03:08,174
You thieving cat!

24
00:03:09,230 --> 00:03:12,160
I-I'm a weasel! I wonder why.

25
00:03:18,343 --> 00:03:21,960
This place is amazing. There's so much stuff here.

26
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:29,580
No, no. Don't get distracted. Straight to the tool shop.

27
00:03:30,131 --> 00:03:32,514
Let's see, where's the tool shop...

28
00:03:38,870 --> 00:03:40,520
Watch out! Get out of the way!

29
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:51,528
Clack-clack, that's so cool.

30
00:03:52,340 --> 00:03:54,708
But pushing me aside and not even apologizing...

31
00:03:54,994 --> 00:03:56,360
All right!

32
00:03:58,460 --> 00:03:59,460
Hey, you!

33
00:03:59,660 --> 00:04:00,660
What?

34
00:04:04,124 --> 00:04:06,680
Where is First Street?

35
00:04:07,034 --> 00:04:10,020
How should I know? I always ride in a carriage.

36
00:04:11,650 --> 00:04:15,270
Hey, that was dangerous! I almost got hit by a bus!

37
00:04:15,860 --> 00:04:19,240
That's because you were daydreaming, country bumpkin.

38
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:20,680
What's a country bumpkin?

39
00:04:20,860 --> 00:04:22,120
It means an idiot.

40
00:04:22,599 --> 00:04:23,599
What did you say?

41
00:04:24,475 --> 00:04:25,014
Chikaro?

42
00:04:25,130 --> 00:04:26,360
Let's go!

43
00:04:28,230 --> 00:04:30,260
Who on earth was that guy?

44
00:04:30,905 --> 00:04:32,740
First Street isn't that way!

45
00:04:33,755 --> 00:04:36,144
You're supposed to go straight to the tool shop!

46
00:04:36,220 --> 00:04:38,120
That's why I'm looking for the way!

47
00:04:38,275 --> 00:04:40,447
And I'm telling you that's the wrong way!

48
00:04:40,765 --> 00:04:42,309
I can go this way too!

49
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:47,033
Mokku, the city is full of strange folks. You'll never get anywhere if you let them bother you!

50
00:04:47,420 --> 00:04:49,477
Come on, hurry up and finish your errand!

51
00:04:50,225 --> 00:04:55,563
I know that. But he is going somewhere. I'll keep an eye on him for a bit.

52
00:04:55,780 --> 00:04:57,470
Don't worry, it's going to be okay.

53
00:04:58,270 --> 00:05:00,320
Mokku! You can't do that!

54
00:05:10,915 --> 00:05:13,125
Oh, he's eating it. He looks just like a human.

55
00:05:13,660 --> 00:05:16,072
Madame, please have a seat.

56
00:05:16,510 --> 00:05:19,151
Chikaro is as cute as ever.

57
00:05:19,175 --> 00:05:21,640
He's quite a handful with his mischief.

58
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:25,680
Chikaro, go play in the garden for a bit.

59
00:05:27,100 --> 00:05:28,100
Yes.

60
00:05:36,980 --> 00:05:37,980
Hey, you!

61
00:05:39,365 --> 00:05:42,360
Hey there, country bumpkin. Still lost?

62
00:05:42,510 --> 00:05:46,057
I followed you here. You're not human, are you?

63
00:05:46,370 --> 00:05:49,600
I am a chimpanzee, an ape far superior to humans!

64
00:05:49,914 --> 00:05:51,635
Are apes really superior to humans?

65
00:05:51,659 --> 00:05:55,380
Apes were born into this world long before humans ever were!

66
00:05:56,336 --> 00:06:00,667
But humans can make all kinds of things and seem to do anything.

67
00:06:00,839 --> 00:06:05,680
Humans just multiply like rats and do everything through sheer numbers.

68
00:06:05,783 --> 00:06:11,579
We ape kind prefer living peacefully in Mother Nature. Who are you, anyway?

69
00:06:12,250 --> 00:06:13,250
You're made of wood, huh?

70
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:18,838
Yeah. Just a wooden puppet. Though I want to become a human.

71
00:06:18,862 --> 00:06:20,967
Why would a puppet want to become a human?

72
00:06:21,610 --> 00:06:25,183
Huh? Do you have any idea how much puppets get made fun of?

73
00:06:25,540 --> 00:06:32,500
Hmm, I-I see. If you became a real human—no, something even greater than human, everyone would be amazed.

74
00:06:32,700 --> 00:06:39,139
Forget being more than human, just being human is enough! You know so much, so please, teach me about humans.

75
00:06:39,945 --> 00:06:42,220
I really don't like dealing with troublesome things.

76
00:06:42,244 --> 00:06:43,120
Hey wait!

77
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:48,200
There's no greater teacher than you! Please!

78
00:06:48,604 --> 00:06:49,740
Take me as your apprentice...

79
00:06:58,389 --> 00:07:00,759
I'm pretty strict. Are you sure about this?

80
00:07:04,808 --> 00:07:06,808
I'm so glad I came to town!

81
00:07:07,714 --> 00:07:09,159
Thief!

82
00:07:09,237 --> 00:07:11,644


83
00:07:13,980 --> 00:07:16,380
You idiot! Run, quick!

84
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:17,720
Right away, Brother!

85
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:18,800
Wait!

86
00:07:19,129 --> 00:07:20,129
Brother!

87
00:07:23,770 --> 00:07:24,770
Hanamuro, stop!

88
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,000
That's enough!

89
00:07:28,170 --> 00:07:30,260
I'm sorry, they got away.

90
00:07:31,780 --> 00:07:32,780
Who are you?

91
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:36,460
I'm Mokku. Starting today, I'm Mr. Chikaro's apprentice.

92
00:07:37,840 --> 00:07:38,840
Chikaro's apprentice?

93
00:07:39,520 --> 00:07:40,520
Yes.

94
00:07:43,580 --> 00:07:50,320
Well, how interesting. All right. If you're Chikaro's apprentice, you're more than welcome. Come on inside.

95
00:07:50,850 --> 00:07:52,260
Thank you very much.

96
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:15,800
(Children screaming)

97
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:23,300
What on earth are you doing? This is how you play the piano.

98
00:08:25,640 --> 00:08:27,680
(Children screaming)

99
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:52,940
(Music)

100
00:08:53,339 --> 00:08:55,720
Such wonderful music.

101
00:08:57,769 --> 00:09:00,060
(Music)

102
00:09:03,919 --> 00:09:05,860
This is the power of amateur music!

103
00:09:05,861 --> 00:09:12,740
This is the primal cry. The rhythm of our monkey clan.

104
00:09:28,079 --> 00:09:29,079
Stop it!

105
00:09:32,709 --> 00:09:34,740
Stop that! Such vulgar music!

106
00:09:37,439 --> 00:09:39,720
You've been a bad boy lately, haven't you?

107
00:09:40,319 --> 00:09:42,960
Isn't it because you took this strange puppet as an apprentice?

108
00:09:47,489 --> 00:09:54,680
Making me out to be the bad guy... Acting so refined when you don't know anything... Seriously! We were just having fun!

109
00:09:55,995 --> 00:10:02,760
*Sigh*... I am sorry... You get carried away way too easily. You'll never rule the world like that.

110
00:10:03,155 --> 00:10:04,460
Go cool your head!

111
00:10:05,020 --> 00:10:06,020
Yes, sir.

112
00:10:11,709 --> 00:10:13,340
What does "catching lightning" mean?

113
00:10:18,265 --> 00:10:20,380
And what good does cooling my head do?

114
00:10:27,329 --> 00:10:28,620
Oh, you guys!

115
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:31,480
Hey, Hanaguro, Mokku's got some real skill, doesn't he?

116
00:10:31,481 --> 00:10:36,820
Sure does. Managed to slip right into a huge mansion.

117
00:10:37,040 --> 00:10:41,100
And when you think about it, that's thanks to us. Right, Mokku? You get that, don't you?

118
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:47,480
Heh-heh-heh, 'cause we pulled off that theft back then, you get to live such a nice life.

119
00:10:47,944 --> 00:10:50,200
What did you guys come to town for?

120
00:10:50,355 --> 00:10:53,480
There are lots of humans in town. Lots of humans means lots of food.

121
00:10:53,580 --> 00:10:55,440
Heh-heh-heh, wonder why.

122
00:10:55,820 --> 00:10:58,740
Then why don't you go look for food in town?

123
00:10:59,660 --> 00:11:01,080
This is someone else's place.

124
00:11:01,279 --> 00:11:03,840
But isn't this your home, too?

125
00:11:04,345 --> 00:11:08,960
I'm just an apprentice, so... Take that!

126
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:10,000
Yah!

127
00:11:10,950 --> 00:11:12,360
You'd better cool off!

128
00:11:12,660 --> 00:11:16,560
I did cool off, but they're crazy about that monkey on the train!

129
00:11:17,115 --> 00:11:19,140
Monkeys are totally outdated!

130
00:11:19,510 --> 00:11:21,320
Outdated? That's not true!

131
00:11:21,800 --> 00:11:23,500
That's right! You'll see!

132
00:11:23,540 --> 00:11:27,480
They can't run as fast as us, their senses aren't sharp, and they don't even blow foul air!

133
00:11:27,679 --> 00:11:31,640
Besides, when we die, we leave our hides behind. What the hell do they do?

134
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:34,000
So that makes you guys better?

135
00:11:34,505 --> 00:11:38,440
Naturally. How about you bring us something to eat?

136
00:11:38,880 --> 00:11:39,880
No way!

137
00:11:41,879 --> 00:11:45,180
Hey, Boss, should we use our usual trick?

138
00:11:45,375 --> 00:11:49,480
Huh?!

139
00:11:52,560 --> 00:11:53,560
(Laughs)

140
00:11:55,820 --> 00:11:57,040
B-B...

141
00:11:59,859 --> 00:12:01,880
Hey, I hear Mokku is weak against fire!

142
00:12:02,140 --> 00:12:07,760
If you don't bring us food, this house might just burn down while you and Sara are asleep!

143
00:12:08,420 --> 00:12:10,080
Boo-hoo!

144
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:12,240
(Laughs)

145
00:12:12,241 --> 00:12:16,640
Getting three meals a day for us should be easy enough, right, little Mokku?

146
00:12:17,629 --> 00:12:20,320
A-All right. I'll bring it.

147
00:12:20,605 --> 00:12:23,960
Our hideout is behind the flowerbed. We'll be waiting, Mokku.

148
00:12:37,689 --> 00:12:39,640
Where could Mokku have gone?

149
00:12:40,605 --> 00:12:45,100
Did he get lost, or did someone take him away?

150
00:12:46,999 --> 00:12:53,100
It was too much for him to go alone... Yes, I'll go to town, too.

151
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:07,300
We're going to Mrs. Shiraishi's party today, so let's get all dressed up.

152
00:13:07,989 --> 00:13:10,240
Mokku, get the bath ready for Caro.

153
00:13:13,689 --> 00:13:17,140
I heard foxes and weasels run faster than you.

154
00:13:17,460 --> 00:13:21,380
So what? Lower animals are the ones that have to run and jump around.

155
00:13:22,040 --> 00:13:27,700
They prey on anything weaker than them, and have to run for their lives the moment they see something stronger.

156
00:13:28,520 --> 00:13:31,260
So that's why they're always running away in such a hurry.

157
00:13:31,565 --> 00:13:32,565
They?

158
00:13:32,685 --> 00:13:35,700
Yeah, some old acquaintances of mine.

159
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:37,360
I see.

160
00:13:43,089 --> 00:13:47,640
Don't waste your time on worthless fools. We're going to become a species more advanced than humans.

161
00:13:48,785 --> 00:13:50,260
I just want to be human.

162
00:13:50,720 --> 00:13:52,020
Aim higher.

163
00:13:52,490 --> 00:13:54,640
I don't care about aiming high, I just want to quit doing this.

164
00:13:54,805 --> 00:13:56,220
You've gotten quite rebellious lately.

165
00:13:56,899 --> 00:14:00,480
It's not that, but are monkeys really better than humans?

166
00:14:00,860 --> 00:14:02,320
Are you mocking me?

167
00:14:02,880 --> 00:14:05,440
No, no, of course not...

168
00:14:09,569 --> 00:14:12,440
Something's off with that Mokku.

169
00:14:13,495 --> 00:14:14,580
Cake! Cake! Cake!

170
00:14:23,569 --> 00:14:25,460
Let's go. Mokku, not bad, huh?

171
00:14:29,860 --> 00:14:32,460
Boss, Mokku brought it.

172
00:14:32,609 --> 00:14:36,640
Oh, Mokku, good job, good job.

173
00:14:37,189 --> 00:14:38,580
Here, it's cake.

174
00:14:39,205 --> 00:14:41,200
Boss, what about drinks?

175
00:14:41,740 --> 00:14:45,660
Oh, right. Hey, there's wine, isn't there? Go on.

176
00:14:46,014 --> 00:14:49,520
It should be in the cellar. You know what'll happen if you don't bring it.

177
00:14:52,349 --> 00:14:53,520
All right.

178
00:14:53,700 --> 00:14:54,700
Here you go.

179
00:15:11,305 --> 00:15:12,300
(Shielding from the sun)

180
00:15:12,301 --> 00:15:13,100
(Sinister male voice)

181
00:15:13,101 --> 00:15:15,241
Thank you. (Sinister male voice)

182
00:15:17,589 --> 00:15:21,001
Ah, so that's what you're doing. No good. (Sinister male voice)

183
00:16:03,149 --> 00:16:04,660
Karon! Help!

184
00:16:05,319 --> 00:16:07,360
Karon! Karon! Karon!

185
00:16:13,965 --> 00:16:15,780
Help me! Come on, listen to me!

186
00:16:16,025 --> 00:16:18,340
You really tricked your way into this house, didn't you!

187
00:16:18,790 --> 00:16:22,520
Just wait, I'll toss you into the fireplace along with the junk! Prepare yourself!

188
00:16:23,420 --> 00:16:31,140
That's the thing! They said they'd burn the whole house down, so I gave them food... As if I'd fall for such a cheap act!

189
00:16:31,539 --> 00:16:34,940
I'd rather throw it away than feed petty thieves like them!

190
00:16:35,899 --> 00:16:38,080
Damn it...

191
00:16:39,599 --> 00:16:41,800
Mokku, how are your accommodations?

192
00:16:42,909 --> 00:16:44,360
Hikaron! Let me out, hurry!

193
00:16:44,870 --> 00:16:48,480
Ending up as firewood is your destiny. Just give up.

194
00:16:48,700 --> 00:16:51,780
Won't you even try to save your apprentice?

195
00:16:52,440 --> 00:16:55,460
I was a fool to trust a wooden puppet.

196
00:16:56,260 --> 00:16:59,920
Now then, I'll head to the party and tease those noble ladies.

197
00:17:00,669 --> 00:17:02,180
Caro! Help me!

198
00:17:02,605 --> 00:17:05,220
Caro! Caro!

199
00:17:13,109 --> 00:17:14,109
Solly!

200
00:17:26,844 --> 00:17:32,720
Don't cry, little lady. I'll scold him soundly later. Shall we dance?

201
00:17:49,440 --> 00:17:50,440
Still alive and kicking.

202
00:17:52,639 --> 00:17:55,580
No, no, wake up.

203
00:17:57,139 --> 00:17:59,140
Who gave you permission to come here...?

204
00:17:59,640 --> 00:18:03,040
Filthy bastard! I won't even speak to him! You talk to him!

205
00:18:03,264 --> 00:18:06,120
Right! Mother got in the way!

206
00:18:06,439 --> 00:18:09,460
If I'm not here, Mother will starve! Just get out!

207
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,540
Idiot! What are you talking about?!

208
00:18:12,740 --> 00:18:15,140
Next time, you bring the food!

209
00:18:15,759 --> 00:18:17,320
Like hell I'd do that for you!

210
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:20,800
Don't act so high and mighty, you monkey bastard!

211
00:18:21,325 --> 00:18:22,325
Shall we get him?

212
00:18:22,799 --> 00:18:24,020
Get him!

213
00:18:24,124 --> 00:18:25,260
Spin, spin, spin, spin, spin!

214
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:28,540
Stop that at once!

215
00:18:28,889 --> 00:18:29,920
Shut up!

216
00:18:50,124 --> 00:18:51,240
This is terrible!

217
00:18:51,544 --> 00:18:53,480
They've come for revenge!

218
00:18:59,300 --> 00:19:00,300
(monkey screeches)

219
00:19:07,099 --> 00:19:08,540
Damn it...

220
00:19:12,264 --> 00:19:13,440
What is it?

221
00:19:16,279 --> 00:19:17,380
Boss!

222
00:19:18,844 --> 00:19:20,080
Goodbye!

223
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:31,700
How dare you humiliate me at the party! In the end, you're nothing but a savage monkey. You're better suited as a circus clown.

224
00:19:42,009 --> 00:19:47,380
Damn it, let me out of the shed! What's your problem? This is awful!

225
00:19:49,705 --> 00:19:54,380
I don't want this! I don't want to be sold to the circus! Stop it!

226
00:19:54,969 --> 00:19:57,300
Am I going to be burned?

227
00:20:10,549 --> 00:20:11,620
Mokku! By apprenticing to a monkey...

228
00:20:12,659 --> 00:20:18,720
...did you become a bit more like one? / No! I'm going to become human! Hurry and take off these chains!

229
00:20:18,864 --> 00:20:21,720
Just mimicking the look and shape of a human is not enough.

230
00:20:22,859 --> 00:20:25,700
Strength is a good example. Do you understand?

231
00:20:26,179 --> 00:20:27,960
Then what am I supposed to do?

232
00:20:28,454 --> 00:20:31,960
You must not rush. You need to build yourself up step by step.

233
00:20:32,779 --> 00:20:34,060
What do you mean, step by step?

234
00:20:34,559 --> 00:20:37,720
You must experience many things and learn about the world.

235
00:20:38,649 --> 00:20:42,820
And once you learn to tell right from wrong, you will be able to become human.

236
00:20:43,739 --> 00:20:48,400
It will be hard. But you must never give up, Mokku.

237
00:20:53,020 --> 00:20:57,800
[[NO AUDIO]]

238
00:21:07,919 --> 00:21:09,940
I don't want to be in the circus.

239
00:21:10,139 --> 00:21:15,340
You're good at the piano and acrobatics, the circus audience will love you. No, no way!

240
00:21:16,279 --> 00:21:20,240
I'll be burned to ashes before I ever find a human heart.

241
00:21:22,220 --> 00:21:23,400
Yeah.

242
00:21:26,320 --> 00:21:27,320
Yeah.

243
00:21:27,719 --> 00:21:34,081
Aaaargh! Huh?!

244
00:21:35,640 --> 00:21:43,900
Ha ha ha! This is a fine monkey! Ha ha ha!

245
00:21:44,584 --> 00:21:46,620
Ha ha ha!

246
00:21:52,619 --> 00:21:55,160
Well then, ma'am, I'll be taking the monkey.

247
00:21:55,600 --> 00:22:02,740
Take him away already. Looking at such a filthy monkey will upset my sweet little Marianne. Won't it, dear?

248
00:22:07,374 --> 00:22:11,420
I don't want to be a circus freak! Mokku, do something!

249
00:22:12,160 --> 00:22:13,160
Geez...

250
00:22:15,544 --> 00:22:18,940
No, no! Save me, Mokku!

251
00:22:19,554 --> 00:22:21,680
Mokku! Mokku!

252
00:22:28,419 --> 00:22:31,680
Hikaron, you're full of energy.

253
00:22:33,459 --> 00:22:34,480
Ma'am!

254
00:22:36,744 --> 00:22:40,900
Don't treat animals like toys. Please truly care for them.

255
00:22:53,719 --> 00:22:56,360
Mokku, is that you, Mokku?

256
00:22:58,084 --> 00:22:59,240
Grandpa.

257
00:23:02,360 --> 00:23:03,360
Mokku.

258
00:23:06,719 --> 00:23:10,940
It's all right now. I don't like seeing that sad face.

259
00:23:11,929 --> 00:23:13,440
Cheer up, Mokku.

260
00:23:14,180 --> 00:23:15,180
Grandpa!

261
00:23:16,749 --> 00:23:19,240
I'm sorry. I'm so useless.

262
00:23:20,144 --> 00:23:23,940
Grandpa made it back, so there's no need to worry.

263
00:23:25,899 --> 00:23:26,900
Grandpa!

264
00:23:33,189 --> 00:23:36,240
Mokku makes friends with an orphaned chick.

265
00:23:37,080 --> 00:23:42,320
To Mokku, this lonely baby stork feels just like a little brother.

266
00:23:43,400 --> 00:23:49,200
One day, the chick is shot and wounded, but survives thanks to the tender care of Mokku and his friends.

267
00:23:50,199 --> 00:23:57,980
Yet as the chick grows day by day, it is destined to grow up and journey to its distant homeland.

268
00:23:58,614 --> 00:24:01,180
Look forward to next week's Kashi no Ki Mokku!

